{"author":{"id":"40e3ba2788b3b9fc163c354afc44e5f9d225bcf0a27e679aaa878dd6135c6dcb"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777790077,"nonce":"G7ZF6wzwShwUM2xgQbU4tyqRoTg=","title":"License audit: verify LGPL-3.0 → GPL-3.0 chain is clean","message":"Before any public outreach (Show HN, Lobsters, software-heritage submission, comp.compression post), audit the license chain to ensure the LGPL-3.0 → GPL-3.0 transition is clean and properly attributed. This is gating for credibility-sensitive audiences who will check.\n\nSpecifically:\n- Identify any code paths in lib/ that originated in Bobrowski's libunuc2 (LGPL-3.0, 2020-2021) and confirm GPL-3.0 relicensing is permitted (LGPL→GPL is a one-way upgrade per LGPL §3, allowed without separate consent).\n- Verify per-file SPDX-License-Identifier headers reflect the correct origin license, not just the project's umbrella GPL-3.0.\n- Confirm CREDITS.md attributes Bobrowski for libunuc2-derived sections specifically, not just as 'inspiration'.\n- Confirm the original 2015 LGPL-3.0 source release by Bezemer is preserved in original/ unchanged with its license header intact.\n- Add a LICENSE-HISTORY.md or similar note explaining the relicensing rationale: which files trace to libunuc2 (LGPL→GPL upgrade), which trace to Bezemer's 2015 LGPL release, and which are new-from-scratch GPL-3.0 work by Valetov.\n- If any code unambiguously came from Bezemer's 2015 LGPL release without modification, decide whether to keep that subset under LGPL or document the relicensing path.\n\nOutput: license-audit.md in docs/ summarizing per-file/per-module provenance, plus updated SPDX headers.","files":null}]}